PROJECT: EtherFi

Strategic Objectives

1. Menjadi protokol liquid restaking terdepan di Ethereum dengan integrasi native EigenLayer dan Symbiotic
· Evidence: EtherFi V2 diluncurkan sebagai "Liquid Restaking Protocol" penuh dengan integrasi native EigenLayer (EV-007, EV-008) dan kemudian menambah Symbiotic (EV-013) — positioning sebagai consumer protocol terbesar di atas EigenLayer
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-007, EV-008, EV-013; Phase 4 Core Components; Phase 7 Major Integrations; Phase 8 Narrative Position

2. Membangun ekosistem multi-chain untuk weETH agar menjadi LRT standar di seluruh L2/L1 EVM
· Evidence: Deployment weETH ke 10+ chain dalam 2 batch (EV-018) — Arbitrum, Optimism, Base, Mode, Blast, Linea, Scroll, zkSync Era, Mantle, BNB Chain — menunjukkan komitmen cross-chain dominance
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-018; Phase 4 Current Technical Stack; Phase 7 External Dependencies (11 chain entries); Phase 8 Market Timeline

3. Mengembangkan produk institusional (Vaults) dan real-world spending (EtherFi Cash) untuk diversifikasi revenue dan user base
· Evidence: EtherFi Vaults launch (EV-011, EV-026) untuk institutional-grade restaking; EtherFi Cash launch (EV-010, EV-023) untuk kartu kredit non-kustodial terhubung ke restaked yield — membuka segmen institusional dan retail tradfi
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-010, EV-011, EV-023, EV-026; Phase 4 Core Components; Phase 5 Revenue Model; Phase 7 Applications

4. Mendesentralisasi governance melalui EtherFi DAO dengan ETHFI token sebagai alignment mechanism
· Evidence: DAO formation post-TGE (EV-017), governance proposals (EV-020, EV-024), fee switch proposal untuk value accrual ke token holder — transisi dari founder-led ke community-governed
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-015, EV-016, EV-017, EV-020, EV-024; Phase 6 Governance; Phase 7 Governance Ecosystem

5. Membangun permissionless operator network (Ultra Light Node) untuk desentralisasi validator set
· Evidence: ULN launch (EV-012) sebagai marketplace permissionless — operator mendaftar tanpa KYC, staker mendelegasikan eETH — mengurangi keandalan pada curated operator set
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-012; Phase 4 Core Components (ULN); Phase 7 Applications; Phase 8 Competitor Landscape (vs Rocket Pool, Puffer)

Decision Timeline

Keputusan: Pendirian EtherFi oleh Mike Silagadze (CEO) dan Rok Kukovec (CTO) (2023)
· Trigger: Identifikasi peluang liquid restaking di Ethereum post-Shanghai/Shanghai upgrade dan EigenLayer emergence
· Evidence: Founder background (Mike Silagadze ex-Top Hat, Rok Kukovec ex-Engineering lead) — Phase 1 Founders, Phase 2 Person entities
· Decision: Mendirikan EtherFi Protocol, memulai pengembangan smart contract eETH/weETH dan integrasi EigenLayer
· Immediate Result: Tim pendiri terbentuk, GitHub repo dipublikasikan (EV-002), seed funding dari Binance Labs, Coinbase Ventures, OKX Ventures (EV-003)
· Long-term Impact: Fondasi seluruh protokol, visi dual restaking layer (EigenLayer + Symbiotic), multi-chain strategy
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 1 Founders; Phase 2 Person entities; Phase 3 EV-001, EV-002, EV-003

Keputusan: Launch Mainnet V1 dengan eETH rebasing token (2023-06)
· Trigger: Ethereum Shanghai upgrade enable withdrawals, EigenLayer testnet live, pasar LST berkembang (Lido stETH dominant)
· Evidence: EV-005 Mainnet V1 Launch — eETH sebagai LST rebasing pertama EtherFi
· Decision: Deploy StakeManager, eETH contract di Ethereum mainnet; user bisa stake ETH → mint eETH
· Immediate Result: eETH live, staking non-kustodial beroperasi, TVL mulai berkumpul
· Long-term Impact: Establish eETH sebagai base layer untuk weETH dan restaking; rebasing mechanism membutuhkan wrapper untuk DeFi composability
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-005; Phase 4 Core Components (eETH); Phase 8 Market Timeline

Keputusan: Deploy weETH (wrapped eETH non-rebasing) untuk DeFi composability (2023-07)
· Trigger: eETH rebasing tidak kompatibel dengan AMM, lending, vault — perlu ERC-20 standard balance
· Evidence: EV-006 weETH Launch — wrapper contract dengan share/price mechanism
· Decision: Deploy weETH wrapper di Ethereum mainnet; 1 weETH = 1 eETH fixed balance, value appreciation via price
· Immediate Result: weETH kompatibel DeFi, bridging-ready, menjadi primary token untuk multi-chain deployment
· Long-term Impact: weETH menjadi LRT standard cross-chain; eETH tetap untuk native staking; dual token model established
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-006; Phase 4 Core Components (weETH); Phase 7 Major Integrations (multi-chain)

Keputusan: Integrasi native EigenLayer mainnet untuk restaking (2023-08)
· Trigger: EigenLayer mainnet launch, demand untuk restaking yield di atas staking yield
· Evidence: EV-007 EigenLayer Mainnet Integration — StrategyManager/DelegationManager integration
· Decision: Integrasikan eETH/weETH ke EigenLayer AVS via Strategy; delegasikan stake ke operator set
· Immediate Result: Restaking rewards otomatis terakumulasi ke eETH/weETH holder; TVL surge
· Long-term Impact: EtherFi menjadi largest consumer protocol di EigenLayer; dependency kritis pada EigenLayer (single point of failure risk)
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-007; Phase 4 External Dependencies (EigenLayer Critical); Phase 7 External Dependencies; Phase 8 Ecosystem Risks

Keputusan: Upgrade ke EtherFi V2 — Liquid Restaking Protocol modular (2023-11)
· Trigger: V1 architecture limited; perlu modular AVS support, upgradeability, restaking native
· Evidence: EV-008 V2 Launch — blog "EtherFi V2 Liquid Restaking", UUPS proxy pattern, modular AVS
· Decision: Redeploy core contracts dengan UUPS upgradeable proxy; tambah StrategyManager untuk multi-AVS; restaking rewards auto-compound
· Immediate Result: Arsitektur siap multi-AVS (EigenLayer + future Symbiotic); upgradeability via governance timelock
· Long-term Impact: Technical foundation untuk semua produk subsequent (Vaults, ULN, Symbiotic integration); governance-controlled upgrades
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-008; Phase 4 Technical Upgrade History; Phase 4 Security Model (UUPS, Timelock)

Keputusan: Launch EtherFi Cash — kartu kredit non-kustodial (2024-01)
· Trigger: Bridge DeFi yield ke real-world spending; differentiator vs competitor LRT
· Evidence: EV-010 EtherFi Cash Launch — cash.ether.fi, Visa/Mastercard network via payment processor
· Decision: Build smart contract wallet terhubung ke physical/virtual card; spending yield dari restaked ETH/stablecoin
· Immediate Result: Produk RWA/DeFi x TradFi live; revenue stream baru (interchange fee, yield spread)
· Long-term Impact: Ekspansi ke APAC (EV-023); user acquisition beyond crypto-native; regulatory complexity increase
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-010, EV-023; Phase 4 Core Components (EtherFi Cash); Phase 5 Revenue Model; Phase 7 Applications; Phase 8 Narrative Position (RWA)

Keputusan: Launch EtherFi Vaults untuk institutional-grade restaking (2024-02)
· Trigger: Institutional demand untuk managed restaking dengan risk management; competitor (Mellow, Kelp) memiliki vault products
· Evidence: EV-011 Vaults Launch — multi-AVS allocation, risk parameter, withdrawal queue, slashing protection
· Decision: Deploy Vault contracts dengan automated allocation ke EigenLayer + Symbiotic AVS; risk engine on-chain
· Immediate Result: Institutional product live; Vaults v2 (EV-026) dengan strategi baru dan AVS tambahan
· Long-term Impact: Revenue diversification (management fee); AUM growth; regulatory scrutiny potential
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-011, EV-026; Phase 4 Core Components (Vaults); Phase 5 Revenue Model; Phase 7 Applications

Keputusan: Launch Ultra Light Node (ULN) permissionless operator marketplace (2024-02)
· Trigger: Desentralisasi validator set; reduce reliance pada curated operators; competitor Rocket Pool/Puffer memiliki operator networks
· Evidence: EV-012 ULN Launch — operator registry, stake delegation, validator + AVS duty coordination
· Decision: Deploy ULN contracts permissionless; siapa saja bisa register operator, staker delegasikan eETH
· Immediate Result: ~150+ operator registered at launch; desentralisasi validator set dimulai
· Long-term Impact: Slashing risk terdistribusi ke staker; operator performance variance; no KYC/reputation system
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-012; Phase 4 Core Components (ULN); Phase 7 Applications; Phase 8 Ecosystem Risks (Permissionless Operator)

Keputusan: Integrasi Symbiotic sebagai restaking layer alternatif (2024-03)
· Trigger: Diversifikasi dari EigenLayer dependency; Symbiotic launch sebagai competitor restaking layer
· Evidence: EV-013 Symbiotic Integration — Vault/Network integration, delegasi eETH/weETH ke Symbiotic
· Decision: Deploy Symbiotic integration contracts; dual restaking layer architecture (EigenLayer + Symbiotic)
· Immediate Result: Restaking ke Symbiotic AVS live; yield diversification; risk spreading
· Long-term Impact: Reduced single-layer dependency; kompleksitas allocation management meningkat; Vaults harus manage dual-layer risk
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-013; Phase 4 External Dependencies (Symbiotic High); Phase 7 External Dependencies; Phase 8 Competitor Landscape (Symbiotic as partner+competitor)

Keputusan: Integrasi Pendle untuk yield trading eETH/weETH (2024-03)
· Trigger: Demand untuk fixed yield dan yield speculation; Pendle sebagai leading yield trading protocol
· Evidence: EV-014 Pendle Integration — PT/YT markets untuk eETH/weETH
· Decision: Deploy Pendle market contracts untuk eETH/weETH; enable PT (principal) dan YT (yield) trading
· Immediate Result: Fixed yield tersedia untuk staker; yield speculation market live; TVL boost dari Pendle incentives
· Long-term Impact: Yield curve discovery untuk eETH/weETH; additional revenue via Pendle swap fees; composability dengan fixed income DeFi
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-014; Phase 4 Core Components (Pendle Integration); Phase 7 Major Integrations; Phase 8 Narrative Position (Yield Trading)

Keputusan: Token Generation Event ETHFI dan multi-CEX listing simultan (2024-03-18)
· Trigger: Funding untuk DAO treasury, liquidity untuk token, community distribution, investor exit/liquidity
· Evidence: EV-015 TGE, EV-016 Multi-CEX Listing — Binance, Coinbase, OKX, Bybit, Gate.io, KuCoin simultaneous
· Decision: Deploy ETHFI token 1B supply; TGE dengan immediate CEX listing; no public launchpad confirmed
· Immediate Result: ETHFI trading live; ~$300-500M market cap range; DAO governance activated (EV-017)
· Long-term Impact: Token sebagai governance + fee accrual vehicle; CEX dependency untuk liquidity; vesting unlock schedule pressure
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-015, EV-016; Phase 5 Token Sale; Phase 6 TGE, Utility; Phase 8 Trading Markets

Keputusan: Pembentukan EtherFi DAO dan aktivasi on-chain governance (2024-03)
· Trigger: Post-TGE requirement untuk decentralized governance; community ownership narrative
· Evidence: EV-017 DAO Formation — Governor + Timelock contracts, Snapshot off-chain signaling
· Decision: Deploy Governor (token-weighted voting), Timelock (2 hari minimal), Treasury management via DAO
· Immediate Result: Governance live; proposal system aktif; first proposal EV-020 (2024-06)
· Long-term Impact: Protocol upgrades, parameter changes, fee switch via DAO; founder control diluted; timelock delay untuk emergency response
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-017, EV-020; Phase 4 Security Model (Timelock); Phase 6 Governance; Phase 7 Governance Ecosystem

Keputusan: Ekspansi multi-chain weETH ke 10+ L2/L1 (2024-04, 2024-05)
· Trigger: User demand cross-chain DeFi; L2 ecosystem incentives (Arbitrum, Optimism, Base, dll); competitor multi-chain (Bedrock, Swell)
· Evidence: EV-018 Batch 1 (Arbitrum, Optimism, Base, Mode, Blast) dan Batch 2 (Linea, Scroll, zkSync, Mantle, BNB Chain)
· Decision: Deploy weETH contracts per chain; integrate canonical bridge + third-party bridge (LayerZero, Wormhole, Hyperlane)
· Immediate Result: weETH available di 11 chain total; DeFi composability cross-chain; bridge liquidity fragmented
· Long-term Impact: Chain dependency diversification; bridge risk multiplied; supply tracking complexity; L2 foundation grants potential
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-018; Phase 4 System Architecture (Cross-chain); Phase 7 External Dependencies (11 chains); Phase 8 Market Position

Keputusan: Fee switch governance proposal untuk revenue sharing ke ETHFI holder (2024-10)
· Trigger: Token holder demand value accrual; competitor (Lido, Rocket Pool) memiliki fee distribution; DAO maturity
· Evidence: EV-024 Fee Switch Proposal — Snapshot vote untuk activate fee accrual ke ETHFI staker/holder
· Decision: Proposal diajukan ke DAO untuk redirect portion protocol fees (staking, restaking, vault, bridging) ke ETHFI holder
· Immediate Result: Vote completed; implementation status perlu verifikasi on-chain
· Long-term Impact: Jika passed — ETHFI menjadi value accrual token, buy pressure; regulatory risk (security classification); treasury revenue reduced
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-024; Phase 5 Revenue Model (Fee Switch); Phase 6 Utility (Fee Accrual); Phase 7 Governance Ecosystem

Evolution Pattern

Strategi Produk: Dari Single LST → Liquid Restaking Protocol → Multi-product Ecosystem
· 2023 H1: eETH only (LST rebasing) — EV-005
· 2023 H2: weETH wrapper + EigenLayer restaking — EV-006, EV-007
· 2023-11: V2 architecture modular multi-AVS — EV-008
· 2024 Q1: Vaults (institusional) + ULN (operator network) + Cash (RWA) — EV-010, EV-011, EV-012
· 2024 Q2: Symbiotic (dual restaking) + Pendle (yield trading) + DAO + Multi-chain — EV-013, EV-014, EV-017, EV-018
· 2024 H2: AVS specific (EigenDA) + Vaults v2 + Fee switch — EV-021, EV-026, EV-024
· Pola: Layering produk baru di atas core staking/restaking infra; setiap produk target segment berbeda (retail, institusional, operator, tradfi)

Teknologi: Dari Simple Staking Contract → Modular Upgradeable Architecture → Multi-chain + Multi-restaking-layer
· V1: Single StakeManager + eETH rebasing (non-upgradeable assumed)
· V2: UUPS proxy untuk semua core contracts; StrategyManager untuk multi-AVS; modular design
· Multi-chain: weETH deployment per chain dengan bridge contracts; canonical + third-party bridge abstraction
· Dual restaking: EigenLayer StrategyManager + Symbiotic Vault/Network integration contracts terpisah
· Vaults v2: Strategy pattern untuk allocation logic; upgradeable via governance
· Pola: Progressive modularization; upgradeability via DAO; abstraction layers untuk chain/restaking-layer heterogeneity

Tokenomics: Dari No Token → Governance Token (ETHFI) → Fee Accrual Token (Planned)
· Pre-TGE: No token; protocol fees ke treasury (founder/team controlled)
· TGE 2024-03: ETHFI deployed 1B fixed supply; governance utility only
· Post-TGE: DAO governance active; fee switch proposal (EV-024) untuk value accrual
· Vesting: Investor/team unlock schedule berlangsung (EV-028 2025-03 anniversary)
· Pola: Progressive decentralization — token launch after product-market fit; fee switch after DAO maturity; vesting alignment

Governance: Dari Founder-led → DAO-governed dengan Timelock
· 2023: Founder/team multisig control semua parameter
· 2024-03: Governor + Timelock deployed; ETHFI token voting
· 2024-06: First community proposal (EV-020)
· 2024-10: Fee switch proposal (EV-024) — major economic parameter change
· Pola: Gradual power transfer; timelock as safety rail; snapshot signaling before on-chain execution

Ekspansi Chain: Ethereum-only → 11 Chain (Ethereum + 10 L2/L1)
· 2023: Ethereum mainnet only (eETH, weETH, core contracts)
· 2024-04: Batch 1 — 5 major L2 (Arbitrum, Optimism, Base, Mode, Blast)
· 2024-05: Batch 2 — 5 additional (Linea, Scroll, zkSync, Mantle, BNB Chain)
· Pola: Prioritaskan L2 dengan TVL tinggi, incentives besar, canonical bridge mature; BNB Chain sebagai non-EVM L1 expansion

Technical Decision Pattern

Pola 1: Ethereum L1 sebagai Settlement Layer Utama, Multi-chain untuk Execution/Distribution
· Decision Pattern: Semua core contracts (eETH, weETH, ETHFI, StakeManager, Vaults, ULN, Governor) dideploy di Ethereum Mainnet; weETH di-deploy ke L2/L1 sebagai ERC-20 non-rebasing untuk DeFi composability dan bridging
· Evidence: Phase 4 System Architecture — "Layer Settlement: Ethereum Mainnet (L1) — semua smart contract inti dideploy di Ethereum"; "Layer Execution: EVM-compatible chains... weETH di-deploy sebagai ERC-20 non-rebasing di setiap chain"; Phase 3 EV-005, EV-006, EV-018; Phase 7 External Dependencies (Ethereum Critical, 10 L2/L1 High)
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-005, EV-006, EV-018; Phase 4 System Architecture, Core Components; Phase 7 External Dependencies

Pola 2: Dual Restaking Layer Architecture (EigenLayer + Symbiotic) untuk Risk Diversification
· Decision Pattern: Integrasikan kedua restaking layer utama (EigenLayer primary, Symbiotic secondary) secara simultan; Vaults dan ULN mendukung allocation ke keduanya; tidak bergantung single layer
· Evidence: Phase 3 EV-007 (EigenLayer 2023-08), EV-013 (Symbiotic 2024-03); Phase 4 Core Components (EigenLayer Integration, Symbiotic Integration); Phase 7 External Dependencies (EigenLayer Critical, Symbiotic High); Phase 8 Ecosystem Risks (Single Restaking Layer Dependency)
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-007, EV-013; Phase 4 Core Components, External Dependencies; Phase 7 External Dependencies, Ecosystem Risks

Pola 3: UUPS Upgradeable Proxy dengan Governance Timelock untuk Semua Core Contracts
· Decision Pattern: Menggunakan OpenZeppelin UUPS (ERC-1967) pattern untuk StakeManager, Wrapper, Vaults, ULN, Governor; upgrade hanya melalui DAO proposal + 2 hari timelock
· Evidence: Phase 4 Security Model — "Upgradeable Proxy: UUPS (ERC-1967) proxy pattern untuk core contracts... upgrade hanya melalui governance timelock"; "Multi-sig / Timelock: Protocol upgrade... minimal 2 hari timelock"; Phase 3 EV-008 (V2 upgrade), EV-017 (DAO timelock); Phase 4 Technical Upgrade History (11 major upgrades)
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-008, EV-017; Phase 4 Security Model, Technical Upgrade History

Pola 4: Rebase Token (eETH) + Non-rebase Wrapper (weETH) untuk DeFi Compatibility
· Decision Pattern: eETH menggunakan rebasing mechanism (supply increase via rebase); weETH sebagai ERC-20 wrapper dengan share/price mechanism (fixed balance, value appreciation) — memisahkan staking native dari DeFi composability
· Evidence: Phase 4 Core Components — "eETH: ERC-20 rebasing token... supply bertambah via rebase setiap epoch"; "weETH: ERC-20 non-rebasing wrapper... 1 weETH = 1 eETH (fixed balance), nilai meningkat via price appreciation"; Phase 3 EV-005 (eETH), EV-006 (weETH); Phase 4 Known Technical Limitations — "eETH rebasing mechanism tidak kompatibel dengan sebagian besar DeFi protocol... memerlukan weETH wrapper"
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-005, EV-006; Phase 4 Core Components, Known Technical Limitations

Pola 5: Permissionless Operator Marketplace (ULN) daripada Curated Operator Set
· Decision Pattern: Membangun Ultra Light Node sebagai permissionless registry — operator mendaftar tanpa KYC/permission, staker mendelegasikan eETH ke operator pilihan mereka, operator menjalankan validator + AVS duties
· Evidence: Phase 3 EV-012 (ULN Launch); Phase 4 Core Components (ULN Marketplace Contract); Phase 7 Applications (ULN Marketplace); Phase 8 Ecosystem Risks — "Permissionless Operator Set (ULN)... operator permissionless tanpa KYC/reputation — staker bear risk operator performance/slashing"; Phase 8 Competitor Landscape (vs Rocket Pool curated, Puffer validator tickets)
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-012; Phase 4 Core Components; Phase 7 Applications; Phase 8 Ecosystem Risks, Competitor Landscape

Pola 6: Canonical Bridge + Third-party Bridge Abstraction untuk Cross-chain weETH
· Decision Pattern: Tidak memaksa single bridge standard; mendukung canonical bridge (Optimism Portal, Arbitrum Bridge, Base Bridge) untuk security dan third-party bridge (LayerZero, Wormhole, Hyperlane) untuk speed/finality; user/integrator pilih bridge
· Evidence: Phase 4 System Architecture — "Cross-chain Messaging: Canonical bridge... + third-party bridge (LayerZero, Wormhole, Hyperlane)... detail implementasi per-chain tidak dipublikasikan secara terpusat"; Phase 7 External Dependencies (LayerZero, Wormhole, Hyperlane Medium); Phase 4 Known Technical Limitations — "weETH bridging mengandalkan canonical bridge (7 hari withdrawal)... atau third-party bridge dengan trust assumptions tambahan"
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-018; Phase 4 System Architecture, Known Technical Limitations; Phase 7 External Dependencies

Pola 7: Foundry sebagai Primary Development Framework dengan Extensive Testing
· Decision Pattern: Menggunakan Foundry (Forge, Cast, Anvil) untuk development, testing, fuzzing, deployment; Hardhat sebagai legacy/alternative; extensive audit program (8 audit firms) sebelum/ setelah deployment
· Evidence: Phase 4 Development Framework — "Foundry (Forge, Cast, Anvil) — smart contract development, testing, deployment, fuzzing (HIGH)"; "Hardhat — legacy/alternative tooling (MEDIUM)"; Phase 4 Audit History — 8 audit firms (Spearbit, Trail of Bits, OpenZeppelin, Sigma Prime, Halborn, Pashov, Code4rena, Cantina) semua completed dengan findings addressed
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 4 Development Framework, Audit History

Financial Decision Pattern

Pola 1: Strategic VC Funding dari Exchange-affiliated Ventures (Binance Labs, Coinbase Ventures, OKX Ventures)
· Decision Pattern: Seed/Private round 2023 didanai oleh venture arm dari 3 CEX terbesar (Binance, Coinbase, OKX) — bukan traditional VC; menyediakan capital + strategic value (listing pipeline, liquidity support, ecosystem access)
· Evidence: Phase 3 EV-003 (Funding Round); Phase 5 Funding History — "Lead Investor: Binance Labs; Participating: Coinbase Ventures, OKX Ventures"; Phase 2 Investor entities (Binance Labs, Coinbase Ventures, OKX Ventures); Phase 5 Financial Dependencies — "VC: Binance Labs, Coinbase Ventures, OKX Ventures — seed/private capital, strategic support, liquidity via exchange listing"
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 2 Investor entities; Phase 3 EV-003; Phase 5 Funding History, Financial Dependencies

Pola 2: Token Generation Event dengan Immediate Multi-CEX Listing (No Public Launchpad Confirmed)
· Decision Pattern: TGE 2024-03-18 dengan simultaneous listing di 6 CEX (Binance, Coinbase, OKX, Bybit, Gate.io, KuCoin) — mengskip traditional launchpad/IDO; immediate liquidity dan price discovery di CEX
· Evidence: Phase 3 EV-015 (TGE), EV-016 (Multi-CEX Listing); Phase 5 Token Sale — "Public Sale: TGE 2024-03-18 — token tersedia untuk trading di Binance, Coinbase, OKX, Bybit, Gate.io, KuCoin... Launchpad: Tidak dikonfirmasi"; Phase 6 TGE — "Launch Platform: Binance, Coinbase, OKX, Bybit, Gate.io, KuCoin (simultaneous CEX listing)"; Phase 8 Trading Markets — 6 CEX live
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-015, EV-016; Phase 5 Token Sale; Phase 6 TGE; Phase 8 Trading Markets

Pola 3: Multi-stream Revenue Model dari Protocol Fees (Staking, Restaking, Vault, Bridging, Cash) + Grant Income
· Decision Pattern: Membangun 8 revenue stream: staking fee, restaking fee, vault management fee, bridging fee, EtherFi Cash revenue, fee switch (proposed), MEV/validator revenue, grant/ecosystem incentive — diversifikasi dari single staking fee
· Evidence: Phase 5 Revenue Model — 8 nama revenue stream dengan status Live/Planned; Phase 3 EV-010 (Cash), EV-011 (Vaults), EV-018 (Bridging), EV-024 (Fee Switch); Phase 7 Major Integrations (CEX listing fees tidak direct tapi liquidity); Phase 8 Narrative Position (RWA, Institutional, Yield Trading)
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-010, EV-011, EV-018, EV-024; Phase 5 Revenue Model; Phase 7 Major Integrations; Phase 8 Narrative Position

Pola 4: Ecosystem Grants dari L2 Foundations dan Restaking Layers sebagai Non-dilutive Funding
· Decision Pattern: Menerima grants dari EigenLayer Foundation, Symbiotic Foundation, dan 10+ L2 foundations (Arbitrum, Optimism, Base, Mode, Blast, Linea, Scroll, zkSync, Mantle, BNB Chain) untuk weETH deployment incentives dan liquidity mining
· Evidence: Phase 5 Funding History — "Funding Round: Ecosystem Grants... Lead: EigenLayer Foundation, Symbiotic Foundation, L2 Foundations"; Phase 7 External Dependencies (11 chain entries semua High/Medium); Phase 8 Market Timeline (EV-018 multi-chain deployment batch 1&2); Phase 5 Financial Dependencies — "Grant Program: L2 Foundation Grants... weETH deployment incentives, liquidity mining"
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-018; Phase 5 Funding History, Financial Dependencies; Phase 7 External Dependencies; Phase 8 Market Timeline

Pola 5: DAO Treasury Management via Governance (Fee Switch Proposal untuk Value Accrual)
· Decision Pattern: Protocol fees terkumpul di DAO treasury; governance proposal (EV-024) untuk mengaktifkan fee switch — redirect portion fees ke ETHFI token holder/staker sebagai value accrual mechanism
· Evidence: Phase 3 EV-024 (Fee Switch Proposal); Phase 5 Revenue Model — "Fee Switch / Protocol Revenue Sharing ke ETHFI Token Holder (Governance-activated fee accrual) — Status: Planned / Governance Proposal"; Phase 6 Utility — "Fee Accrual (Fee Switch)... Status: Planned / Governance Proposal"; Phase 7 Governance Ecosystem (DAO manages treasury)
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-024; Phase 5 Revenue Model; Phase 6 Utility; Phase 7 Governance Ecosystem

Pola 6: Tidak Memublikasikan Financial Transparency Data (Treasury, Revenue, Vesting Detail)
· Decision Pattern: Tidak ada transparency report berkala, treasury dashboard, revenue historical data, token distribution breakdown, vesting schedule detail — semua financial detail "tidak diungkap" atau "tidak dipublikasikan"
· Evidence: Phase 5 Treasury — "Current Treasury Size: tidak diungkap... Treasury Composition: tidak diungkap"; Phase 5 Revenue History — "Tidak diungkap... tidak mempublikasikan laporan pendapatan berkala"; Phase 6 Distribution — semua kategori "tidak diungkap persentase pasti"; Phase 6 Vesting Schedule — semua kategori "tidak diungkap"; Phase 5 Financial Risk — "Treasury Concentration: Treasury composition tidak diungkap"
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 5 Treasury, Revenue History, Financial Risk; Phase 6 Distribution, Vesting Schedule

Ecosystem Decision Pattern

Pola 1: Deep Integration dengan EigenLayer sebagai Primary Restaking Layer (Critical Dependency)
· Decision Pattern: Build seluruh restaking logic di atas EigenLayer (StrategyManager, DelegationManager, AVS Registry); eETH/weETH sebagai largest consumer protocol TVL di EigenLayer; AVS-specific integration (EigenDA) sebagai value-add
· Evidence: Phase 3 EV-007 (EigenLayer Integration), EV-021 (Specific AVS); Phase 4 External Dependencies (EigenLayer Critical); Phase 7 External Dependencies (EigenLayer Critical); Phase 7 Major Integrations (EigenLayer Mainnet + Specific AVS); Phase 8 Ecosystem Risks (Single Restaking Layer Dependency); Phase 8 Competitor Landscape (EigenLayer sebagai dependency DAN partner)
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-007, EV-021; Phase 4 External Dependencies; Phase 7 External Dependencies, Major Integrations, Ecosystem Risks; Phase 8 Competitor Landscape

Pola 2: Multi-chain Expansion via weETH Deployment ke Semua Major L2/L1 EVM
· Decision Pattern: Systematic deployment weETH ke 11 chain (Ethereum + 10 L2/L1) dalam 2 batch terstruktur; prioritas chain dengan TVL tinggi, canonical bridge mature, ecosystem incentives; bridge abstraction untuk user
· Evidence: Phase 3 EV-018 (Batch 1: Arbitrum, Optimism, Base, Mode, Blast; Batch 2: Linea, Scroll, zkSync, Mantle, BNB Chain); Phase 4 System Architecture (11 chain listed); Phase 7 External Dependencies (11 chain entries High/Medium); Phase 7 Major Integrations (Batch 1 + Batch 2); Phase 8 Market Timeline (EV-018 milestones)
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-018; Phase 4 System Architecture; Phase 7 External Dependencies, Major Integrations; Phase 8 Market Timeline

Pola 3: Strategic Partnerships dengan DeFi Primitives (Pendle untuk Yield Trading, Chainlink untuk Oracle)
· Decision Pattern: Integrasi dengan category-leading DeFi protocols sebagai complementary primitives — Pendle untuk yield trading (PT/YT), Chainlink untuk price feeds/oracle — bukan build sendiri
· Evidence: Phase 3 EV-014 (Pendle Integration); Phase 4 External Dependencies (Chainlink High); Phase 7 Major Integrations (Pendle Integration); Phase 7 External Dependencies (Chainlink High); Phase 8 Narrative Position (Yield Trading Secondary)
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-014; Phase 4 External Dependencies; Phase 7 Major Integrations, External Dependencies; Phase 8 Narrative Position

Pola 4: Real-world Bridge via EtherFi Cash (Payment Network + Stablecoin Custodian)
· Decision Pattern: Partnership dengan traditional payment rails (Visa/Mastercard via processor) dan stablecoin custodian untuk enable spending yield di dunia nyata — bridge DeFi ke TradFi
· Evidence: Phase 3 EV-010 (Cash Launch), EV-023 (Cash Expansion); Phase 4 Core Components (EtherFi Cash); Phase 7 Major Integrations (EtherFi Cash Payment Network Integration); Phase 7 External Dependencies (Visa/Mastercard network inferred); Phase 8 Narrative Position (RWA/DeFi x TradFi Secondary)
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-010, EV-023; Phase 4 Core Components; Phase 7 Major Integrations, External Dependencies; Phase 8 Narrative Position

Pola 5: CEX Listing Strategy dengan Exchange-affiliated Investors (Binance, Coinbase, OKX) + Tier-1 Exchanges
· Decision Pattern: Leverage investor relationships (Binance Labs, Coinbase Ventures, OKX Ventures) untuk securing major CEX listings; expand ke Bybit, Gate.io, KuCoin untuk geographic coverage (Asia) dan derivatives (perpetual)
· Evidence: Phase 3 EV-016 (6 CEX listing); Phase 2 Investor entities (Binance Labs, Coinbase Ventures, OKX Ventures); Phase 7 Exchange Ecosystem (6 CEX + Uniswap); Phase 8 Trading Markets (6 CEX live, 5 dengan perpetual); Phase 5 Financial Dependencies (VC provide liquidity via exchange listing)
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 2 Investor entities; Phase 3 EV-016; Phase 7 Exchange Ecosystem; Phase 8 Trading Markets; Phase 5 Financial Dependencies

Pola 6: Infrastructure Dependencies pada Established Providers (GitHub, Vercel, Dune, Etherscan, Chainlink, Alchemy/Infura)
· Decision Pattern: Menggunakan best-in-class infrastructure providers untuk hosting, CI/CD, analytics, block explorer, oracle, RPC — tidak build in-house infrastructure
· Evidence: Phase 7 Infrastructure Providers (11 providers); Phase 4 Current Technical Stack (GitHub Actions CI/CD, Vercel hosting, Dune analytics, Chainlink oracle); Phase 7 External Dependencies (GitHub High, Vercel High, Dune Medium, Etherscan/Arbiscan/Optimistic Etherscan/Basescan High, Chainlink High)
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 4 Current Technical Stack; Phase 7 Infrastructure Providers, External Dependencies

Governance Decision Pattern

Pola 1: Progressive Decentralization — Founder Control → DAO Governance dengan Timelock
· Decision Pattern: Mulai dari founder/team multisig control (2023), deploy Governor + Timelock post-TGE (2024-03), first community proposal (2024-06), major economic proposal fee switch (2024-10) — transfer power bertahap dengan safety rails
· Evidence: Phase 3 EV-017 (DAO Formation), EV-020 (First Proposal), EV-024 (Fee Switch); Phase 4 Security Model (Timelock 2 hari minimal); Phase 6 Governance (On-chain DAO, token-weighted, delegation, 2-day timelock); Phase 7 Governance Ecosystem (DAO, no council/committee)
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-017, EV-020, EV-024; Phase 4 Security Model; Phase 6 Governance; Phase 7 Governance Ecosystem

Pola 2: Token-weighted Voting dengan Off-chain Signaling (Snapshot) + On-chain Execution
· Decision Pattern: Gunakan Snapshot untuk off-chain signaling (gasless voting), Governor contract untuk on-chain execution via Timelock — delegasi voting power didukung
· Evidence: Phase 6 Governance — "Voting System: Token-weighted voting (1 ETHFI = 1 vote) — snapshot off-chain signaling + on-chain execution"; "Delegation: Supported"; Phase 3 EV-020, EV-024 (Snapshot proposals); Phase 7 Governance Ecosystem (Snapshot + On-chain)
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-020, EV-024; Phase 6 Governance; Phase 7 Governance Ecosystem

Pola 3: Governance Parameter Control — Protocol Fees, Risk Parameters, Upgrades via DAO
· Decision Pattern: DAO mengontrol parameter ekonomi (fee switch EV-024), vault risk parameters, protocol upgrades via UUPS proxy, treasury management — founder tidak bisa unilateral change
· Evidence: Phase 3 EV-024 (Fee Switch), EV-026 (Vaults v2 upgrade via governance); Phase 4 Technical Upgrade History (11 upgrades, beberapa via governance); Phase 4 Security Model (UPGRADER_ROLE, Timelock); Phase 6 Governance (Treasury Governance via DAO)
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-024, EV-026; Phase 4 Technical Upgrade History, Security Model; Phase 6 Governance

Pola 4: Minimal Governance Structure — No Council, No Committee, Pure Token Voting
· Decision Pattern: Tidak ada governance council, committee, atau delegated body — semua keputusan via token-weighted voting semua ETHFI holder; Snapshot untuk signaling, Governor untuk execution
· Evidence: Phase 7 Governance Ecosystem — "Council: tidak diketahui — tidak ada council terpisah"; "Committee: tidak diketahui — tidak ada committee resmi"; Phase 6 Governance (token-weighted voting semua holder)
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 6 Governance; Phase 7 Governance Ecosystem

Pola 5: Emergency Response via PAUSER_ROLE (Multi-sig/DAO) bukan Governance Vote
· Decision Pattern: Untuk critical bug/exploit, menggunakan PAUSER_ROLE (multi-sig/DAO controlled) untuk pause contracts — tidak butuh governance vote + timelock; upgrade tetap butuh timelock
· Evidence: Phase 4 Security Model — "Pausability: Pausable (OpenZeppelin) pada core contracts — emergency pause oleh PAUSER_ROLE (multi-sig/DAO)"; "Governance timelock minimal 2 hari — memperlambat emergency response untuk critical bug"; Phase 8 Ecosystem Risks (Governance Timelock Delay)
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 4 Security Model; Phase 8 Ecosystem Risks

Risk Response Pattern

Pola 1: Proactive Multi-layer Audit Strategy untuk Smart Contract Risk Mitigation
· Decision Pattern: Melakukan 8 audit dari firm berbeda (Spearbit, Trail of Bits, OpenZeppelin, Sigma Prime, Halborn, Pashov, Code4rena, Cantina) mencakup core, vaults, ULN, bridge, cash, governance — sebelum dan setelah deployment; competitive audit (Code4rena, Cantina) untuk fresh eyes
· Evidence: Phase 4 Audit History — 8 audit firms dengan tanggal, scope, status "Completed — findings addressed"; Phase 4 Security Model (Audit Coverage HIGH); Phase 8 Ecosystem Risks (Smart Contract Risk HIGH)
· Trigger: Smart contract exploit risk (TVL >$3B, high value target)
· Response: Comprehensive audit program covering setiap major release; audit reports published di github.com/etherfi-protocol/audits
· Result: Tidak ada major exploit terlapor hingga 2025-01; findings addressed per audit
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 4 Audit History, Security Model; Phase 8 Ecosystem Risks

Pola 2: Dual Restaking Layer (EigenLayer + Symbiotic) untuk Single-layer Dependency Risk
· Decision Pattern: Integrasi Symbiotic (EV-013) sebagai alternatif EigenLayer — diversifikasi AVS exposure, slashing risk spreading, negotiating leverage
· Evidence: Phase 3 EV-013 (Symbiotic Integration); Phase 4 External Dependencies (EigenLayer Critical, Symbiotic High); Phase 7 External Dependencies (both High); Phase 8 Ecosystem Risks (Single Restaking Layer Dependency, Alternative Restaking Layer Dependency)
· Trigger: EigenLayer single point of failure risk (exploit, slashing massal, regulatory action)
· Response: Build Symbiotic integration parallel; Vaults allocate ke dual-layer; ULN operators support both
· Result: Risk diversification achieved; complexity increased (dual allocation logic, dual withdrawal queues)
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-013; Phase 4 External Dependencies; Phase 7 External Dependencies, Ecosystem Risks

Pola 3: Permissionless Operator Set (ULN) dengan Slashing Risk Terdistribusi ke Staker
· Decision Pattern: ULN permissionless tanpa KYC/reputation — operator risk (performance, slashing, MEV extraction) fully borne oleh staker yang mendelegasikan; tidak ada insurance fund atau slashing coverage terverifikasi
· Evidence: Phase 3 EV-012 (ULN Launch); Phase 4 Core Components (ULN); Phase 7 Applications (ULN); Phase 8 Ecosystem Risks (Permissionless Operator Set — "staker bear risk operator performance/slashing... tanpa recourse"); Phase 8 Competitor Landscape (vs Rocket Pool curated, Puffer validator tickets)
· Trigger: Desentralisasi validator set requirement; avoid curated operator centralization
· Response: Permissionless registry; staker choose operator; slashing socialized ke delegator
· Result: ~150+ operator registered; high decentralization; staker sophistication required
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-012; Phase 4 Core Components; Phase 7 Applications; Phase 8 Ecosystem Risks, Competitor Landscape

Pola 4: Bridge Abstraction (Canonical + Third-party) untuk Cross-chain Risk Distribution
· Decision Pattern: Tidak mandate single bridge; support canonical (slow, secure) dan third-party (fast, additional trust) — user/integrator pilih risk profile; bridge contracts per chain terpisah
· Evidence: Phase 4 System Architecture (Cross-chain Messaging); Phase 4 Known Technical Limitations (Bridge dependency); Phase 7 External Dependencies (LayerZero, Wormhole, Hyperlane Medium); Phase 8 Ecosystem Risks (Bridge Dependency — "bridge hack = loss of funds cross-chain")
· Trigger: Cross-chain interoperability requirement; no single bridge dominates security/speed
· Response: Abstract bridge layer; deploy weETH per chain dengan multiple bridge options
· Result: Bridge risk distributed; user choice; supply tracking fragmented; no unified bridge TVL dashboard
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 4 System Architecture, Known Technical Limitations; Phase 7 External Dependencies; Phase 8 Ecosystem Risks

Pola 5: Governance Timelock (2 hari) + PAUSER_ROLE untuk Emergency Response Balance
· Decision Pattern: 2 hari timelock untuk upgrade/parameter change (security), PAUSER_ROLE multi-sig untuk instant pause (emergency) — trade-off responsiveness vs security
· Evidence: Phase 4 Security Model (Timelock 2 hari, Pausable PAUSER_ROLE); Phase 8 Ecosystem Risks (Governance Timelock Delay — "memperlambat emergency response"); Phase 3 EV-017 (DAO Timelock)
· Trigger: Need upgradeability + emergency stop capability
· Response: UUPS proxy + Timelock untuk planned changes; Pausable + PAUSER_ROLE untuk emergencies
· Result: Secure upgrade path; emergency pause capability; but upgrade delay remains untuk non-pause fixes
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 3 EV-017; Phase 4 Security Model; Phase 8 Ecosystem Risks

Pola 6: Regulatory Uncertainty Management via Legal Opacity (No Public Legal Entity/Compliance Disclosure)
· Decision Pattern: Tidak mempublikasikan legal entity jurisdiction, foundation status, regulatory engagement, compliance framework — opacity sebagai strategy untuk regulatory flexibility
· Evidence: Phase 1 Country/Legal Entity "tidak diketahui"; Phase 2 Entity "EtherFi Foundation — struktur belum diverifikasi publik (LOW)"; Phase 5 Financial Risk (Legal Financial Risk MEDIUM); Phase 8 Open Threads (Regulatory status, legal entity jurisdiction)
· Trigger: Regulatory uncertainty di DeFi/staking/restaking (SEC stance, MiCA, dll)
· Response: Minimal public disclosure; DAO sebagai governance vehicle; foundation status ambiguous
· Result: Flexibility maintained; but institutional adoption barrier; investor due diligence harder
· Supporting Dataset: Phase 1 Country/Legal Entity; Phase 2 Entity (EtherFi Foundation); Phase 5 Financial Risk; Phase 8 Open Threads

